/* 

  Number of records for permutations and normal distribution in Picat.

  How many records are there in a sequence of n elements?

  This calculates the probabilities of the number of records for n values.

  The theoretical values is quite good for permutations and continuous
  distributions. For discrete distributions, e.g. uniform discrete, binomial, etc,
  this does not apply. (I'm still trying to find out theories for these distributions.)

  The mean is the harmonic_number(N).

  Cf my Gamble model gamble_record_number_of_records.rkt

  This program was created by Hakan Kjellerstrand, hakank@gmail.com
  See also my Picat page: http://www.hakank.org/picat/

*/

import ppl_distributions, ppl_utils.
import util.
% import ordset.

main => go.

/*

  n = 10
  PDF:
   1 0.1 
   2 0.282896825396825 
   3 0.323164682539683 
   4 0.199426807760141 
   5 0.07421875 
   6 0.017436342592593 
   7 0.002604166666667 
   8 0.000239748677249 
   9 0.000012400793651 
  10 0.000000275573192 

  Sorted by prob:
   3 0.323164682539683 
   2 0.282896825396825 
   4 0.199426807760141 
   1 0.1 
   5 0.07421875 
   6 0.017436342592593 
   7 0.002604166666667 
   8 0.000239748677249 
   9 0.000012400793651 
  10 0.000000275573192 

  CDF:
   1 0.1 
   2 0.382896825396825 
   3 0.706061507936508 
   4 0.905488315696649 
   5 0.979707065696649 
   6 0.997143408289242 
   7 0.999747574955908 
   8 0.999987323633157 
   9 0.999999724426808 
  10 1.0 

  Quantile:
  0.000001  1 
  0.00001  1 
  0.001  1 
  0.01  1 
  0.025  1 
  0.05  1 
  0.1  1 
  0.25  2 
  0.5  3 
  0.75  4 
  0.84  4 
  0.9  4 
  0.975  5 
  0.99  6 
  0.999  7 
  0.99999  9 
  0.999999  9 

  Mean: = 2.92897
  Mean (h_n): = 2.92897

*/
go ?=>
  N = 10, % 10 value in the list
  println(n=10),
  println("PDF:"),
  [V=num_records_dist_pdf(N,V)  : V in 1..N].printf_list,
  nl,
  println("Sorted by prob:"),
  [V=num_records_dist_pdf(N,V)  : V in 1..N].sort_down(2).printf_list,  
  nl,
  println("CDF:"),
  [V=num_records_dist_cdf(N,V)  : V in 1..N].printf_list,
  nl,
  println("Quantile:"),
  [Q=num_records_dist_quantile(N,Q)  : Q in quantile_qs()].printf_list,
  nl,
  println("Mean:"=num_records_dist_mean(N)),
  println("Mean (h_n):"=num_records_dist_mean_h_n(N)),  
  
  nl.
go => true.

